PulseAudio RAOP: answer a HomePod's timing requests from ANNOUNCE on, and take timing_port=0.

A HomePod (AirTunes 980) sends NTP timing requests to the sender's timing port as soon as it gets SETUP,
and replies to SETUP only once they are answered: after 30 s without, it fails SETUP with 500. Stock
PulseAudio opens the port at ANNOUNCE but its sink thread polls it only after the SETUP reply, when the
socket is connected. Until then the main loop now answers, with recvfrom/sendto.

The reply then says timing_port=0 (the receiver takes no timing requests), which stock PulseAudio fails
on; the timing socket is connected to the port the receiver asked from instead.

--- a/src/modules/raop/raop-client.c
